# /etc/rosy/host-guard/hosts.conf on the guarding host (D-530). Host-local: it holds addresses,
# so only this template is tracked. Quiet window = the target's nightly reboot (rosy-nightly-reboot.timer)
# from 10 min before to 20 min after; "-" means none.
# <name> pc <user>@<tailnet-address> <HH:MM-HH:MM>
# <name> robot <lan-address>:<core-port>
# <name> updates <user>@<address>   (D-871: update channels only, no recovery ladder; e.g. this PC's own user)
model pc <user>@<model-pc-address> 05:53-06:23
ai pc <user>@<ai-pc-address> 05:48-06:18
robot-a robot <robot-a-address>:8080
robot-b robot <robot-b-address>:8080
site updates <site-user>@127.0.0.1
# <name> monitoring <https-url> [<ca-file>]   alert through the webhook when R Monitoring's /monitoring-health fails or its last_success is older than GUARD_MONITORING_STALE_MIN (15)
#   ALERT_AFTER checks in a row (it carries no last-success time, so only the status code is checked), e.g.:
# r-monitoring monitoring https://<site>.local/monitoring-health /etc/rosy/host-guard/site-ca.crt
# One more pc line per OMX cell control PC, e.g.: cell-b pc <user>@<cell-b-address> 05:40-06:10
# rosy-arm-cell (role cell) is guarded from R, never by itself: its own host-guard stays off. Add its line only after
# its rosy-host-control helper matches D-991 (reboot refused during an arm session); the guard ladder reboots otherwise.
# On the model PC (reverse guard of the site PC), the file holds one line:
# site pc <user>@<site-pc-address> 05:58-06:28
# D-1021 drift lines (needs the current rosy-host-guard-remote on the target): <time_source> is the site map's, "-" skips the
# name compare; after it, the retired host names (full names, from the site map) to look for in chrony and /etc/hosts.
# One line per PC; the site PC's own line lets the OTHER guard see this guard stop (guard-age):
# model drift <user>@<model-pc-address> <ntp-name> <retired-name>
# site drift <user>@<site-pc-address> <upstream-a>,<upstream-b>,<upstream-c> <retired-name>
# On the site PC, the Account login probe's report (rosy-site-account-login-check writes it; alerts on a failure streak and recovery):
# account-login logincheck /var/lib/rosy-account-login-check/status.json
